   "source": [
    "##### 1.2.2.1 Decode HTML entities\n",
    "\n",
    "Implementation: `html.unescape` from the standard library converts every HTML entity\n",
    "in one pass. This handles named entities (`&amp;` -> `&`), numeric entities\n",
    "(`&#39;` -> `'`), and named character references in a single call - we don't have to\n",
    "maintain our own table of mappings."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 748,
   "id": "59",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def decode_html_entities(text: object) -> str:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Decode HTML entities. e.g. &amp; -> &, &#39; -> '\"\"\"\n",
    "    if text is None:\n",
    "        return \"\"\n",
    "    return unescape(str(text))"
   ]
  },
