   "source": [
    "_PUNCT_TABLE = str.maketrans(\n",
    "    string.punctuation.replace('-', '').replace(\"'\", \"\"),\n",
    "    ' ' * len(string.punctuation.replace('-', '').replace(\"'\", \"\")),\n",
    ")\n",
    "def remove_punctuation(text: object) -> str:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Replace punctuation with spaces, preserving hyphens and apostrophes.\"\"\"\n",
    "    if text is None:\n",
    "        return \"\"\n",
    "    return str(text).translate(_PUNCT_TABLE)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "74",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "##### 1.2.2.9 Remove diacritics\n",
    "\n",
    "Implementation: NFD Unicode decomposition splits a character like `é` into the base\n",
    "letter `e` plus a combining acute accent. We then drop every combining mark\n",
    "(those for which `unicodedata.combining(c)` is non-zero), leaving the bare ASCII letter."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 756,
   "id": "75",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def remove_diacritics(text: object) -> str:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Strip accent marks. e.g. café -> cafe, naïve -> naive\"\"\"\n",
    "    if text is None:\n",
    "        return \"\"\n",
    "    return ''.join(\n",
    "        c for c in unicodedata.normalize('NFD', str(text))\n",
    "        if not unicodedata.combining(c)\n",
    "    )"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "76",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "##### 1.2.2.10 Remove round brackets\n",
    "\n",
    "Implementation: two `str.replace` calls, one for `(` and one for `)`. We replace with\n",
    "the empty string because the words inside the brackets are already separated from\n",
    "neighbouring text by spaces."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 757,
   "id": "77",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def remove_round_brackets(text: object) -> str:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Strip ( and ) characters.\"\"\"\n",
    "    if text is None:\n",
    "        return \"\"\n",
    "    return str(text).replace('(', '').replace(')', '')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "78",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "##### 1.2.2.11 Remove URLs\n",
    "\n",
    "Implementation: regex `https?://\\S+|www\\.\\S+` matches both `http(s)://...` and\n",
    "`www....` URLs, where `\\S+` greedily consumes everything up to the next whitespace.\n",
    "We replace the match with the empty string."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 758,
   "id": "79",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def remove_urls(text: object) -> str:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Remove http://, https://, and www. links.\"\"\"\n",
    "    if text is None:\n",
    "        return \"\"\n",
    "    return re.sub(r'https?://\\S+|www\\.\\S+', '', str(text))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "80",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "##### 1.2.2.12 Remove emojis\n",
    "\n",
    "Implementation: we use `emoji.replace_emoji(text, replace='')` from the third-party\n",
    "`emoji` library. This library knows about every emoji code point (including ZWJ\n",
    "sequences and skin-tone modifiers) so we don't have to maintain our own ranges."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 759,
   "id": "81",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def remove_emojis(text: object) -> str:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Remove all emoji characters from text.\"\"\"\n",
    "    if text is None:\n",
    "        return \"\"\n",
    "    return emoji.replace_emoji(str(text), replace='')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "82",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "##### 1.2.2.13 Normalise Unicode\n",
    "\n",
    "Implementation: NFKD decomposition (similar to NFD but also splits compatibility\n",
    "characters like ligatures), followed by an `encode('ascii', 'ignore').decode('ascii')`\n",
    "round-trip that drops anything outside the ASCII range. This is the final safety net -\n",
    "anything left after the previous steps that is still non-ASCII gets stripped here."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 760,
   "id": "83",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def normalize_unicode(text: object) -> str:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Normalise Unicode to ASCII. e.g. 𝙄𝙩'𝙨 -> It's. Non-ASCII chars are dropped.\"\"\"\n",
    "    if text is None:\n",
    "        return \"\"\n",
    "    return (\n",
    "        unicodedata.normalize('NFKD', str(text))\n",
    "        .encode('ascii', 'ignore')\n",
    "        .decode('ascii')\n",
    "    )"
   ]
  },
